WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.082
By the end of this module, you should be able to identify long and wide structures,

00:00:05.082 --> 00:00:10.582
pivot and unpivot data in PostgreSQL, and explain the grain of each result.

00:00:10.582 --> 00:00:18.592
You should also be able to detect when a reshape changes more than structure because aggregation or a

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:19.097
join has altered the facts.

00:00:19.097 --> 00:00:26.437
Finally, you should be able to choose a shape based on what happens next: visualization, reporting,

00:00:26.437 --> 00:00:31.502
or modeling. Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:31.502 --> 00:00:35.752
a survey project reshaping question responses for analysis.

00:00:35.752 --> 00:00:42.667
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:46.052
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:46.052 --> 00:00:50.127
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:50.127 --> 00:00:55.967
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:55.967 --> 00:01:00.080
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
